2026-06-03 14:18:46,771 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Attack Narrative
2026-06-03 14:18:46,771 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The domain controller was running an **internet-facing IIS web server** hosting www.stark-research-labs.com — a critical security misconfiguration. Multiple **webshell signatures** (ASP, PHP, JSP, Perl) were detected in memory, indicating the web server was likely compromised via web exploitation (T1190). **RemCom** (a remote command execution tool) was also loaded in memory, providing post-exploitation capability. The **w3wp.exe** IIS worker process showed code injection (malfind), confirming active webshell execution.
2026-06-03 14:18:46,773 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **PsExec.exe** and a full SysInternals suite were deployed at C:\Tools\ and subsequently **deleted** (TSK shows reallocated inodes), consistent with either legitimate admin cleanup or anti-forensics. **Mimikatz** references on the companion workstation (10.3.58.5, connected to the DC via SMB) suggest credential harvesting may have occurred in the environment.
