2026-06-03 14:44:26,221 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] | # | Finding | Severity | Confidence |
2026-06-03 14:44:26,221 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] |---|---------|----------|------------|
2026-06-03 14:44:26,222 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] | 1 | **Event Logs Cleared** — Security (128 MB) and System (7.1 MB) EVTX files are empty. Same anti-forensics pattern as nromanoff workstation. | HIGH | Confirmed |
2026-06-03 14:44:26,223 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] | 2 | **Synchronized Group Policy Modification** — GroupPolicy directories modified at identical timestamp (2012-04-03 20:38:07) on both nfury and nromanoff. Precedes malware deployment by 25 min. | HIGH | Confirmed |
2026-06-03 14:44:26,224 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] | 3 | **Clean Process/Network State** — No malware, no suspicious processes, no C2 at capture time. System was rebooted between attack window (2012-04-03-04) and capture (2012-04-06), clearing volatile evidence. | MEDIUM | Inference |
2026-06-03 14:44:26,225 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] | 4 | **RDP Sessions Detected** — Two prior RDP sessions recovered via psscan: investigator session (2012-03-15) and post-compromise session (2012-04-04 with cmd.exe usage). | MEDIUM | Confirmed |
2026-06-03 14:44:26,226 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] | 5 | **Normal User Activity** — nfury user shows standard browsing, no malware signatures on disk/memory. Targeted by domain-level attack but no direct malware artifacts found on this host. | INFO | Confirmed |
2026-06-03 14:44:26,227 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Answers to Investigation Questions
2026-06-03 14:44:26,228 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 1. **Suspicious processes?** No — all 36 processes at capture time are legitimate (Windows, McAfee, VMware, F-Response). No malfind shellcode, no YARA hits.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,228 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 2. **External/C2 connections?** No — only F-Response forensic acquisition (to 10.3.16.5) and standard domain traffic to DC (10.3.58.4).
2026-06-03 14:44:26,229 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 3. **Program execution evidence?** Limited — Prefetch files exist on disk including some deleted entries (EXPLORER.EXE, FIREFOX SETUP, DLLHOST.EXE). Prefetch parser failed during extraction.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,230 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 4. **Persistence mechanisms?** The Group Policy Machine\Scripts modification at 2012-04-03 20:38 is the primary persistence indicator, representing domain-level GPO-based execution.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,230 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 5. **Lateral movement?** RDP was enabled (port 3389 listening) with two prior sessions detected. SMB/LDAP connections to DC observed. The session on 2012-04-04 18:17 occurred the day after the GP modification.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,231 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 6. **Defense evasion?** YES — Event logs systematically cleared on this system (same as nromanoff), and system rebooted before forensic acquisition.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,232 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 7. **User accounts?** nfury (primary user), rsydow (also logged in per disk evidence). No SAM-level anomalies detected.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,233 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 8. **YARA/Sigma/Hayabusa?** No malware signatures detected on the nfury system, unlike the nromanoff and DC systems.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,233 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 9. **IOCs?** No malicious IOCs extracted from nfury disk — normal browsing URLs (Facebook, LinkedIn, Microsoft, Google).
2026-06-03 14:44:26,234 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 10. **Deleted files?** ~387,507 deleted entries found (mostly ProgramData and Users churn), no suspicious targeted deletions like the SysInternals toolkit found on the DC.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,235 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 11. **EVTX analysis?** Both Security and System logs are empty — anti-forensics.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,236 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 12. **Data exfiltration?** No evidence of data staging or exfiltration on nfury.
2026-06-03 14:44:26,236 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Conclusion
2026-06-03 14:44:26,237 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The nfury workstation was clearly within the scope of the domain-wide compromise — evidenced by cleared event logs and synchronized Group Policy modification — but **no direct malware artifacts** were found on this host. The attacker likely had access via domain credentials (same GP push affecting both workstations) but focused active exploitation on the nromanoff workstation (TopLZAGU.exe, mimikatz) and the domain controller (webshells, RemCom). The system reboot before forensic capture eliminated any volatile evidence that might have existed.
