2026-06-03 15:07:09,712 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ## XP System (10.3.58.7 / WKS-WINXP32BIT / tdungan) — Investigation Summary
2026-06-03 15:07:09,713 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### 1. Malicious Processes in Memory
2026-06-03 15:07:09,715 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Zeus/Zbot rootkit confirmed** in two critical system processes:
2026-06-03 15:07:09,716 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - **services.exe (PID 676)**: 22 API hooks across ntdll.dll, USER32.dll, WS2_32.dll, CRYPT32.dll, and WININET.dll — all redirecting to injected `<unknown>` module code
2026-06-03 15:07:09,717 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - **lsass.exe (PID 688)**: 4 API hooks in ntdll.dll (NtCreateThread, NtQueryDirectoryFile + Zw variants)
2026-06-03 15:07:09,719 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### 2. Code Injection Evidence
2026-06-03 15:07:09,720 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Confirmed.** All Zeus hooks are inline/trampoline JMP patches redirecting to code in unmapped memory regions. This constitutes active code injection into services.exe and lsass.exe. The hooking module is `<unknown>` — not any loaded DLL — proving injected shellcode.
2026-06-03 15:07:09,722 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### 3. Network Connections
2026-06-03 15:07:09,723 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - **SMB connection from DC (10.3.58.4:58562) → XP (10.3.58.7:445) CLOSED** — lateral movement vector
2026-06-03 15:07:09,724 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - **WebDAV connections from XP → DC** on port 80 with Microsoft-WebDAV-MiniRedir/5.1.2600 user agent (2011-08 through 2012-03)
2026-06-03 15:07:09,726 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Zeus WININET hooks actively intercept all HTTP traffic for credential harvesting
2026-06-03 15:07:09,727 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### 4. Hidden/Unlinked Processes
2026-06-03 15:07:09,729 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] XP system uses Windows XP SP3, which has limited psscan/pslist comparison capability. No explicit hidden process evidence found in the precooked data. The Zeus rootkit hides via NtQueryDirectoryFile hooks (file hiding) rather than process unlinking.
2026-06-03 15:07:09,730 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### 5. MBR Modification
2026-06-03 15:07:09,731 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **No bootkit detected.** MBR strings show standard boot messages: "Invalid partition table", "Error loading operating system", "Missing operating system". Binwalk also returned no embedded content.
